   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## Forms that grow out of the wall\n\n**kubakub height animate** takes a height map (black = the wall, white = furthest out) and lets it grow: one height map per frame, and the same as a relief lit from the side, laid on `image`.\n\nHere the height comes from **kubakub form height** (the sample building with a sample form; see `form_height.json` for your own model). It can be **any depth map** instead: connect the output of Depth Anything or Marigold to `height`, the picture it was made from to `image`, and raise `wall` to the grey of the wall so only what stands in front of it grows.\n\n- `grow`: all together, peaks first, built up in layers, or along the field (connect a kubakub mask field, e.g. radial or a drawn direction).\n- `curve`: ramp grows once; sine breathes; beats / hits and sound level follow a sound on `audio`.\n- `scale` is 0.5 here to keep it quick.\n\n`height` (the grey frames) goes into the depth presets of kubakub shader (hard shadow) or out as displacement; `lit` is a ready clip, also as the guide of kubakub motion guide."
   ],
   "title": "Read me"
  }
